    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d581">

                <pb facs="0656" n="644" sameAs="frus:frus1944v03/pg644"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851.01/3342: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Acting American Representative to the French Committee of National
                        Liberation</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Chapin</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-01-17T16:00:00-04:00">January 17, 1944—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>161. Please draft an appropriate acknowledgment to Committee’s note of January 8
                    quoted in your 129, January 12, and state that its contents have been brought to
                    the attention of the competent military authorities of the United States.</p>
                <p>For your information the matter has been referred to Admiral Leahy<anchor n="10"
                        xml:id="d581-f1"/> for information of and consideration by Joint Chiefs of
                    Staff.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d581-f1" n="10" xml:id="d581-f1-content">
                <p>Adm. William D. Leahy, Chief of Staff to the Commander in Chief of the Army and
                    Navy.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
